  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "What is $1.5%$ of $60?$",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $60,$ and the percentage is $1.5%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n1.5%=1.5÷100=0.015\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =1.5%\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.015\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n1.5%=\\frac{1.5}{100}=\\frac{1.5\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{15}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =1.5%\\times 60 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{1,000}\\times 60 \\\\  & =\\frac{900}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$",
